          "text": "{\n  \"code\": \"R = 29.0\\nheight = 84.0\\nseam = 0.31\\nhalf_width = math.pi * R\\n# Sample true developed coordinates at less than 0.10 mm spacing.\\nx = np.linspace(-half_width - 0.5, half_width + 0.5, 1901)\\ny = np.linspace(-height/2 - 0.5, height/2 + 0.5, 901)\\nU = x[None, :]\\nV = y[:, None]\\ntheta = seam + (U + half_width)/R\\nX = R * np.cos(theta)\\nY = R * np.sin(theta)\\nZ = V + height/2\\n# Positive inside the uncut rectangular sheet.\\nfield = np.minimum(half_width - np.abs(U), height/2 - np.abs(V))\\nbores = [([5.0, 0.0, 37.0], [1.0, 0.37, 0.61], 12.0),\\n         ([-4.0, 7.0, 62.0], [0.24, 1.0, -0.32], 8.0)]\\nfor point, axis, radius in bores:\\n    n = np.array(axis, dtype=float)\\n    n = n / np.linalg.norm(n)\\n    dx = X - point[0]\\n    dy = Y - point[1]\\n    dz = Z - point[2]\\n    along = dx*n[0] + dy*n[1] + dz*n[2]\\n    distance_squared = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz - along*along\\n    clearance = np.sqrt(np.maximum(distance_squared, 0.0)) - radius\\n    field = np.minimum(field, clearance)\\n# Export filled vector contours in the specified SVG convention.\\nsvg = contour_svg(x, y, field)\",\n  \"explanation\": \"The isometric development is u=29(theta\u22120.31\u2212pi), v=z\u221242, producing a 182.2124 \u00d7 84 mm sheet. Each normalized drill axis defines an infinite cylinder; every surface point whose perpendicular distance to either axis is below its drill radius is removed, including both sides and cuts crossing the seam. Interpolated vector contours use spacing below 0.10 mm for the requested 0.15 mm accuracy. The helper supplies the required viewBox, scale(1,-1) convention, white background and solid black retained material. Execution and SVG generation were checked successfully.\"\n}"
